// Two Go modules, deliberately not one.
//
// api/ is the cloud monolith and agent/ is the booth binary. They share no
// code: the agent talks to the API over the versioned /v1 path, which is the
// only coupling the kiosk record allows, and a shared module would quietly turn
// that into a compile-time one. Outlet #1 will be running a six-month-old
// binary by the time outlet #3 exists, so the two must be able to move apart.
//
// This file exists for editors and for `go test ./...` from the repo root. CI
// builds each module from its own directory.
go 1.26.5

use (
	./agent
	./api
)
